[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113890,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sialolipoma is a neoplastic lipomatous proliferation within salivary glands, with an oncocytic (oncocytic lipoadenoma) or non-oncocytic (sialolipoma) epithelial component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113891,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8850/0 Sialolipoma</p>\r\n<p>8850/0 Oncocytic lipoadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113892,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.0 &amp; XH8P28 Benign neoplasm of parotid gland &amp; Lipoadenoma</p>\r\n<p>2E90.3 &amp; XH8P28 Benign neoplasm of other or unspecified parts of mouth &amp; Lipoadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113893,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> lipoadenoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> adenolipoma; oncocytic sialolipoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113894,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytic lipoadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113895,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Conventional lipomas (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/52/193\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Lipomas</em>) predominate in parotid glands (&ge;&nbsp;80%), whereas sialolipoma and oncocytic lipoadenoma manifest in minor glands (50%) and in parotid glands (40%) {11135044; 20952301; 23401010; 33187016}. In the oral cavity, the lower lip and tongue are the most common locations {33187016}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113896,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a slow-growing swelling. The salivary gland location is verified by radiological or intraoperative localization and/or by histological demonstration of a rim of salivary parenchyma {11135044; 23232852; 23401010}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113897,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mean age at presentation regardless of site is 51.5&nbsp;years, with an equal sex distribution {19347375}. In minor salivary gland cases, the mean age of 10&nbsp;patients was 46.1&nbsp;years (range: 11&ndash;71&nbsp;years) and the M:F&nbsp;ratio was 1:2.3 {33187016}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113898,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113899,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113900,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sialolipomas are well-circumscribed tumours measuring 30&ndash;40&nbsp;mm on average.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113901,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Combined lipoepithelial salivary gland lesions comprise a spectrum of morphological subtypes from sialolipoma to oncocytic lipoadenoma. Sialolipoma combines lobules of salivary parenchyma with dominating and evenly interspersed adipose tissue. The salivary parenchyma rarely shows focal sebaceous differentiation and is usually devoid of oncocytic epithelium. The term &ldquo;sialolipoma&rdquo; indicates that the adipocytic component is regarded as neoplastic {11135044; 20952301; 23232852; 33187016}.</p>\r\n<h5>Subtype</h5>\r\n<p>The rare oncocytic lipoadenoma subtype typically demonstrates a predominance of epithelial elements with a varying oncocytic component, reminiscent of oncocytoma. A minor sebaceous component may occur. The term &ldquo;oncocytic lipoadenoma&rdquo; indicates that the oncocytic/epithelial component is regarded as neoplastic {23232852}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The entities include extrasalivary lipomatous tumours (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/52/190\" target=\"_blank\">section </a>Chapter&nbsp;9: <em>Soft tissue tumours</em>) and epithelial salivary tumours with lipomatous metaplasia, especially pleomorphic adenoma&nbsp;/ myoepithelioma {11787848}, and a fatty replacement (lipomatosis) in atrophic salivary parenchyma secondary to chronic inflammation or old age {11135044; 23232852}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T16:02:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113902,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 72,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytological preparations may show mature adipocytic and salivary epithelial elements in varying proportions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T14:09:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
